<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Kazakhs to hold first 2-yr T-bills auction June 20.</title>
<headline>Kazakhs to hold first 2-yr T-bills auction June 20.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kazakhstan will auction 200 million tenge of two-year MKM discount Treasury bills at their first auction on June 30, the National Bank said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Full details of the two-year issue:</p>
<p>    Series number		  KZ52K0107998</p>
<p>    Issue volume		   200 million tenge</p>
<p>    Denominations		  1,000 tenge</p>
<p>    Tenor			    728 days</p>
<p>    Issue date		     June 30</p>
<p>    Maturity date		  July 1, 1999</p>
<p>In contrast to the existing three-, six- and 12-month T-bills, two-year paper is coupon-bearing. Coupons will be paid twice a year.</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom, +7 3272 509410</p>
</text>
